course: dictionary
lesson: 634
title: Many meanings of background
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so the sentence tells you which one to use. Look at the words around it. «It is usually red on a yellow background» means the part behind the main things, furthest from you.
explain: Background can also mean your family, your culture and where you come from. «A disadvantaged background» means someone grew up poor. When you read a word that could mean two things, ask: which meaning fits here? Then try it in the sentence to check.
explain: «In the background» means present but not the centre of attention. Background noise is quiet sound that is there but not the main thing you listen to.
fact: Background has several meanings, so check the sentence to find the right one.
fact: «Background» can mean the part of a picture or scene furthest from you, as in «her street in the background».
fact: «Your background» means your family, your culture and where you come from.
fact: «In the background» means present but not the centre of attention, like «background music».
fact: On a computer, a program can run «in the background», quietly, while you do something else.
exercise: «It is usually red on a yellow background.» What does background mean here? | A quiet sound you hear | The family someone comes from | *The part behind the main things | The facts you need first
exercise: «Pupils come from many backgrounds, so we learn to respect each other.» What does background mean here? | *Family, culture and where you come from | Music played softly | The part of a picture furthest away | A test you take at the end
exercise: Jayden says a program is running «in the background». What does it mean? | Stopped completely | Being checked by a teacher | Shown at the very front of the screen | *Running quietly while you do something else
test: «AI pictures can have odd backgrounds.» Which meaning fits here? | Facts you need before you start | Quiet music playing softly | *The part behind the people and things in the picture | Where someone comes from
test: Ella says background noise is loud shouting in the centre of the room. Is she right? | Yes, it means the centre of the stage | No, it means complete silence | *No, it is quiet sound in the background, not the centre of attention | Yes, it means loud shouting
exam: «A disadvantaged background» means someone grew up poor. Which sentence uses background in the same way? | We played music in the background at the party | The sky was pale blue behind the hills | *Children from different backgrounds bring different stories to class | The noise in the background stopped at once
